[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2952433509","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105705#issuecomment-2952433509","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105705","id":2952433509,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6v-o9l","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-07T12:33:45Z","updated_at":"2025-06-07T16:16:26Z","body":"This is the result of the polygon layout as the astar path search travels from closest edge point to closest edge point in the direction of the target. That builds the polygon corridor that is later used by whatever path postprocessing is used.\n\nThat the corridor-funnel snaps to the polygon corridor corners just makes the issue with the layout and how astar travels visually more noticeable.\n\nThis is not a bug, it is a general limitation that comes with such navmesh layouts. This and all related layout-sourced issues can only be solved by adding new features like different pathfinding algorithms or line-of-sight checks (apart from the solution of changing the layout).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin